  "answer_text": "In the **2025\u201326 NBA season**, the Indiana Pacers **did not make the playoffs**. Plagued by injuries\u2014most notably star player Tyrese Haliburton missing the entire season due to a torn Achilles tendon\u2014the Pacers finished with a 19\u201363 record. They were the first team in the league to be mathematically eliminated from postseason contention on March 10, 2026. \n\nDepending on which previous playoff run you are referring to, here is who they played:\n\n### **2025 Playoffs (2024\u201325 Season)**\nThe Pacers had a thrilling run all the way to the NBA Finals as the Eastern Conference Champions:\n*   **First Round:** Defeated the **Milwaukee Bucks** (4\u20131)\n*   **Conference Semifinals:** Defeated the **Cleveland Cavaliers** (4\u20131)\n*   **Eastern Conference Finals:** Defeated the **New York Knicks** (4\u20132)\n*   **NBA Finals:** Lost to the **Oklahoma City Thunder** (3\u20134) in a dramatic 7-game series\n\n### **2024 Playoffs (2023\u201324 Season)**\nThe Pacers made an unexpected deep run to the Eastern Conference Finals:\n*   **First Round:** Defeated the **Milwaukee Bucks** (4\u20132)\n*   **Conference Semifinals:** Defeated the **New York Knicks** (4\u20133)\n*   **Eastern Conference Finals:** Lost to the **Boston Celtics** (0\u20134)",
